      "id": "idea",
      "narration": "Meet Rajat Gupta. He rose from the slums of India to run a famous consulting firm, sat on corporate boards, and was worth over one hundred million dollars. By any measure, he had won. But it was not enough. He wanted to be a billionaire, so he leaked secret boardroom tips to a hedge fund manager and landed in federal prison. Bernie Madoff was already a wildly successful, legitimate businessman before he ran the largest fraud in history. Both men had everything, and risked all of it for more they did not even need.",
